            "english_quote": "Since, then, the scriptures themselves speak of many gods and at other times of only one",
            "issue": "The Greek explicitly reports assertions of existence: the scriptures say that there are many gods and elsewhere that there is only one. 'Speak of' weakens these assertions into references or mentions. This matters because the passage distinguishes speaking or naming gods from asserting that they exist, and its concluding accusation depends on the conflicting existential assertions.",
